---
/**
 * ProblemSection — names the pain. PEACE: P + E.
 */
---

<section class="section bg-cumberland-cream">
  <div class="container-rail max-w-4xl">
    <p class="eyebrow">Sound familiar?</p>
    <h2 class="mt-4 text-cumberland-ink">Print shops shouldn't make your job harder.</h2>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-cumberland-stone">
      You've got a deadline. A team that needs to look sharp. A storefront
      that's still a blank wall. A truck that should be working harder for your
      brand. The last thing you need is:
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-lg text-cumberland-ink">
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="mt-1.5 h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-cumberland-clay shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        A national online shop that won't take your call when the order's late.
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="mt-1.5 h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-cumberland-clay shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        A local vendor who ghosts you for a week and then "had a question" about
        your file.
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="mt-1.5 h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-cumberland-clay shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        Five separate suppliers for shirts, banners, signs, and wraps when one
        shop should handle it all.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-8 text-xl italic text-cumberland-forest font-semibold">
      That's not how this should work.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
